TM-085 AC6 — accessibility, responsive and failure-state checks, measured

tests/browser/planner-a11y.mjs, headless Chrome at 390x844:

  ok   no horizontal page scroll at 390px
  ok   the turn grid collapses to one column on phone
  ok   touch targets meet the family floor
  ok   the verbatim refusal wraps instead of clipping
  ok   the live region is announced but not shown
  ok   every section is labelled for a screen reader
  ok   the refused proposal is not colour-only
  ok   every visible control is keyboard reachable
  ok   focus is visible, not suppressed
  ok   nothing animates under prefers-reduced-motion   (measured 1e-05s)

  10 passed, 0 failed

tests/browser/planner.mjs, the approval path:

  ok   the proposal renders as an inspectable card
  ok   the card names a consequence, not just its arguments
  ok   previewing wrote nothing to the board
  ok   the only text input is the one bound to the open question
  ok   approving opens a confirmation
  ok   the confirmation names the digest being approved
  ok   apply is disabled until the review box is ticked
  ok   a click on the disabled control applies nothing
  ok   ticking the box enables apply
  ok   approving applies exactly the proposed change
  ok   and the session ends

  11 passed, 0 failed

One correction along the way: the reduced-motion assertion originally demanded a transition
duration of exactly 0 and failed. The app was right and the test was wrong — the family kill
switch uses 0.01ms rather than 0, because a zero-duration transition can skip its transitionend
event. The assertion now reads "effectively instant".
